  "details": "the origin of the \"joystick\" when you move with your left middle finger doesn't follow you if you rotate in real space, so that causes unexpected behavior for me. when i use quest wirelessly, i prefer to never touch my rotation stick and only rotate with my body. the origin could follow your facing direction by smoothly following the average of your head and your hands. most vr games with things on your chest and waist do this because they don't actually know where your waist is. i can see the origin stays behind me (local space, not world space) when i turn around based on looking at the UI vector.",
